{
  "slug": "retry-storm-propogation",
  "title": "Retry Storm Propagation",
  "description": "How uncontrolled retries amplify outages, and practical patterns: exponential backoff, jitter, limits, timeouts, and idempotent side effects.",
  "keywords": ["retry storm", "exponential backoff", "jitter", "timeouts", "idempotency", "distributed systems"],
  "author": "Pawan Bisht",
  "publishedAt": "2026-09-25",
  "tags": ["retry", "reliability", "distributed-systems"],
  "categories": ["engineering"],
  "readingTimeMinutes": 12,
  "featured": true,
  "relatedSlugs": ["cache", "redundancy"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Retries feel like reliability"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Until everyone starts retrying at the same time. The service goes down:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Request fails",
        "Client retries",
        "Service is still struggling",
        "More requests arrive",
        "More retries happen",
        "Load increases",
        "Service gets even slower",
        "More requests time out",
        "More retries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "richText",
      "html": "Now your <b>reliability mechanism</b> is helping create the outage.<br>This is a retry storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Retries aren't inherently bad"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The problem is retrying without thinking about:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Exponential backoff",
        "Jitter",
        "Maximum retry attempts",
        "Timeouts",
        "Circuit breakers",
        "Idempotency",
        "Which failures should actually be retried"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Why This Is Dangerous"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Suppose 100,000 clients all make a request."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The service fails."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If every client immediately retries:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "100,000 original requests",
        "        ↓",
        "100,000 retries",
        "        ↓",
        "200,000 requests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If those retries fail and everyone retries again:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "200,000",
        "   ↓",
        "200,000 more retries",
        "   ↓",
        "400,000 requests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The retry mechanism can amplify the original problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The important lesson:"
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "text": "A retry is additional traffic. Never think of a retry as \"free.\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Exponential Backoff"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Instead of:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "fail",
        " ↓",
        "retry immediately",
        " ↓",
        "fail",
        " ↓",
        "retry immediately"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Wait progressively longer between attempts."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Attempt 1 → fails",
        "      ↓",
        "wait 100 ms",
        "",
        "Attempt 2 → fails",
        "      ↓",
        "wait 200 ms",
        "",
        "Attempt 3 → fails",
        "      ↓",
        "wait 400 ms",
        "",
        "Attempt 4 → fails",
        "      ↓",
        "wait 800 ms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conceptually:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "delay = base × 2^attempt"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "For example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": ["100ms", "200ms", "400ms", "800ms", "1600ms"]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Usually you also put an upper limit on the delay."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "max delay = 5 seconds"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "So it doesn't grow forever."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Jitter"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Exponential backoff alone isn't always enough."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Imagine 100,000 clients receive the same failure at:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "12:00:00.000"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "They all calculate:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "retry after 100ms"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Then they all retry around:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "12:00:00.100"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Boom. Another traffic spike."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is called a synchronized retry problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Jitter adds randomness to the delay."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Instead of:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Everyone retries after exactly 400ms"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You might get:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Client A → 327ms",
        "Client B → 412ms",
        "Client C → 376ms",
        "Client D → 451ms",
        "..."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Now the retries are spread over time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conceptually:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Exponential backoff",
        "        +",
        "Random jitter",
        "        =",
        "Much safer retry behavior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Maximum Retry Attempts"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Never assume:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "while request fails:\n    retry()"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "That can create an infinite retry loop."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Instead:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Maximum attempts = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Attempt 1",
        "   ↓ fail",
        "Attempt 2",
        "   ↓ fail",
        "Attempt 3",
        "   ↓ fail",
        "STOP"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The system should eventually give up and return an error."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Retries are a mechanism for recovering from temporary failures, not a guarantee that every request must eventually succeed."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Timeouts Are Essential"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A retry without a timeout can be dangerous."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Imagine:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Request",
        "   ↓",
        "Waiting for database",
        "   ↓",
        "30 seconds",
        "   ↓",
        "Still waiting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Now the client retries."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You might have:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Original request → still running",
        "Retry request    → running"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You have doubled the work."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Always think about:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Request timeout",
        "Connection timeout",
        "Database query timeout",
        "Upstream service timeout",
        "Retry delay",
        "Total operation deadline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A useful mental model is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "Total request deadline",
        "        │",
        "        ├── attempt 1",
        "        ├── backoff",
        "        ├── attempt 2",
        "        ├── backoff",
        "        └── attempt 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "All attempts should fit within a reasonable overall deadline."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Not Every Error Should Be Retried"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is one of the most important retry rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "text": "Usually potentially retryable"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Network timeout",
        "Connection reset",
        "Temporary 503",
        "Temporary infrastructure failure",
        "Some 429 responses",
        "Some transient database errors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "text": "Usually NOT retryable"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "400 Bad Request",
        "401 Unauthorized",
        "403 Forbidden",
        "404 Not Found",
        "Invalid input",
        "Validation failure",
        "Business-rule failure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Retrying an invalid request usually doesn't fix anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "For example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "http",
      "code": "POST /users\n\nemail = \"not-an-email\""
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the server returns:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "http",
      "code": "400 Bad Request"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Retrying 5 times doesn't magically make the email valid."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Be Careful With POST and Side Effects"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is where idempotency becomes important."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Suppose:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "http",
      "code": "POST /payments"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The server receives the request:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Charge customer ₹1000"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The payment succeeds."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "But the response gets lost because of a network failure."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The client sees:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "TIMEOUT"
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "text": "The request failed. I'll retry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Now POST /payments runs again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Potentially:"
    },
    {
      "type": "flowDiagram",
      "lines": [
        "₹1000 charged",
        "+",
        "₹1000 charged again",
        "=",
        "₹2000 charged"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The original operation may have succeeded even though the client didn't receive the response."
    }
  ]
}
